From: noname <noname@example.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:59:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: stm32: i2s: reprogram an unusably low kernel clock

stm32_i2s_set_parent_rate() trusts the current kernel clock as soon as
stm32_i2s_rate_accurate() reports it as "accurate".  That helper compares
the maximum expected kernel clock against the current one with
DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST(), so any clock that divides into the maximum passes -
even one that is far too low for the peripheral, which can only divide
the kernel clock down (MCKDIV >= 1, frame length 16/32 bits).

On the STM32MP257F watermelon-wine-1a the CK_KER_SPI2 flexgen comes up at
54857 Hz instead of 6.144 MHz.  54857 * 112 = 6143984, within 2 ppm of
6.144 MHz, so the driver skipped clk_set_rate(); the I2S prescaler then
clamped to divider 1 and the frame clock became ~1.7 kHz, making all
audio play about 28x too slow (and the video, which follows the audio
clock, collapse with it).

Reject a current kernel clock below 32 * fs so the driver programs a
usable rate, exactly as it already does when the accuracy check fails.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: noname <noname@example.com>

--- a/sound/soc/stm/stm32_i2s.c
+++ b/sound/soc/stm/stm32_i2s.c
@@ -424,7 +424,17 @@
 	 * return immediately.
 	 */
 	i2s_curr_rate = clk_get_rate(i2s->i2sclk);
-	if (stm32_i2s_rate_accurate(i2s, i2s_clk_max_rate, i2s_curr_rate))
+	/*
+	 * The I2S peripheral can only divide the kernel clock down again.
+	 * With MCKDIV >= 1 and a frame length of 16/32 bits the kernel clock
+	 * must be at least 32 * fs, but stm32_i2s_rate_accurate() accepts any
+	 * rate that divides into the maximum rate: a kernel clock of 54857 Hz
+	 * passed for 48 kHz because 54857 * 112 ~= 6.144 MHz.  The prescaler
+	 * then clamped to divider 1 and the frame clock fell to ~1.7 kHz, so
+	 * audio played ~28x too slow instead of the clock being reprogrammed.
+	 */
+	if (i2s_curr_rate >= 32 * rate &&
+	    stm32_i2s_rate_accurate(i2s, i2s_clk_max_rate, i2s_curr_rate))
 		return 0;
 
 	/*
